  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering patients for a healthier society - Annual Work Programme 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;em&gt;Overall objective(s) &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1. To improve the status of people living with HIV in North Macedonia by ensuring a more reliable system for provision of contemporary treatment and more effective protection against discrimination&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. To make a significant contribution towards increasing the percentage of people living with HIV who are aware of their HIV-status and linked to care and towards achieving the 2025 UN targets in North Macedonia (so as to set the course for ending AIDS by 2030)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. To strengthen capacities of Stronger Together and other patient organizations to address common structural issues in the national health system that impact access to life-saving medicines and quality of care&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;em&gt;Specific objective(s) &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.1. To ensure an evidence-based approach and transparency of processes related to the provision of antiretroviral medicines, including planning of needs, budgeting and procurement&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.2. To improve the existing mechanisms in the country responsible for protecting against and sanctioning discrimination with regards to addressing the discrimination based on HIV or other health status&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2.1. To increase the up-take of HIV testing services provided by Stronger Together and other civil society organizations within the community of gay and bisexual men, as well as other men who have sex with men&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2.2. To ensure that the national response to HIV is informed by evidence and addresses the key points of concern in the country epidemic&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3.1. To strengthen the overall capacities of the organization to pursue its mission, with a focus on revised accounting and staff policies and building a collaborative approach in addressing structural health-related issues&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
